# /paths shelf: files that never belong on it. gitignore syntax — `*` `?`
# `[...]` within a name, `**` across folders, a trailing `/` = a folder (and
# everything in it), `!pattern` re-includes, the LAST match wins. `~/...` and
# absolute paths work here too. These rules win over every repo's
# .gitignore / .ignore / .rgignore and the global git excludes, which also
# apply. Files you COPY (Finder Cmd+C, a pasted path) skip all of this.
# Edits apply within ~2 s; nothing to restart.

# compiled / generated
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.o
*.obj
*.class
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.d
*.swiftmodule
*.swiftdeps
*.swiftdoc

# editor / OS scratch
*.swp
*.swo
*~
~$*
.DS_Store
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig

# half-done downloads and transfers
*.crdownload
*.part
*.partial
*.download

# app state / files that churn in the background (copy one in Finder to
# shelve it anyway)
*.plist
*.log
*.lock
*.pid
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.db-journal

# build / dependency / cache trees
build/
dist/
target/
out/
.build/
.cache/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
vendor/
coverage/
.venv/
venv/
